./LOGBOOK.md:14:- IMPLEMENTATION: The generated workspace now has a minimal macOS host and one embedded packet-tunnel system extension at `Contents/Library/SystemExtensions/works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel.systemextension`. The host and provider use the r12 identifiers, macOS 15 floor, shared build/protocol version, target-owned plists, and separate Development/Developer ID entitlement files. The provider imports NetworkExtension and implements only empty start/stop plus version-message handling.
./LOGBOOK.md:24:- GATES: Every M0 viability row maps evidence for both candidates. libssh2 has no waived red row; ReluxNIOSSH's missing neutral TCP ownership, opaque signer, bounded intake, algorithm reporting, keepalive, and unbuilt adapter rows remain explicit. The four deferred semantics remain unsupported/notReported under `TASK-260728-3cveay`; physical scale, extension memory, soak, and DNS footprint remain M3 gates.
./LOGBOOK.md:25:- MEASUREMENT: Five consecutive current-tree, already-built real-OpenSSH M0 lifecycle runs exit 0 in 11.058–11.144 s test time. Whole-command maximum RSS is 71,254,016 B and maximum macOS peak footprint is 17,891,952 B; every lifecycle iteration asserts zero channels, socket, session, automatic tasks, custom allocations, and buffered bytes. This is a controlled harness envelope containing direct-tcpip, not an isolated DNS-open p99 or physical extension budget.
./LOGBOOK.md:29:- MAINTENANCE: BSD-3-Clause and Apache-2.0 notices remain mandatory; archive, patch, header, artifact, extension-safety, and negative source gates fail closed. `TASK-260728-3cveay` owns future selected-engine fork/rebase work. Any mandatory red, security advisory, patch-bound breach, platform/server-policy change, or red M3 physical result reopens ADR-014 rather than weakening a gate.
./LOGBOOK.md:49:- TESTS: The candidate-neutral Swift Testing suite dispatches the same M0, cancellation-scope, and M3-deferred inventory from candidate data. The libssh2 row invokes `LibSSH2TransportFactory` through real OpenSSH/loopback adapter tests; ReluxNIOSSH has no `SSHTransport` adapter target and is represented by explicit known-issue rows rather than a green emulated fixture.
./LOGBOOK.md:73:- ORCHESTRATION REWORK: Review found that the first helper only validated declarations. The checked-in provider now provisions task-owned current/fallback macOS sshd profiles, creates the no-mount/no-container Ubuntu Lima row, resolves the approved real-host alias, starts numeric-loopback destinations on each SSH server, enforces task-owned rotation versus real-host owner management, and tears everything down. Every non-success row requires a finite provider control before either candidate driver runs; free-form observation text is rejected. External provider commands remain optional overrides, while the two real candidate drivers stay external because their matrix tasks own candidate verdicts.
./LOGBOOK.md:117:- MATRIX: The real-loopback-sshd libssh2 gate passes 46 tests across adapter, bridge, and provider-contract suites. A new test-only compatibility row forces and verifies both approved transport sets: curve25519/Ed25519/aes256-ctr/hmac-sha2-256 and group14-sha256/P-256/aes128-ctr/hmac-sha2-512. Client byte/time/manual rekey, server-rekey-safe traffic, keepalive transmission, direct/exec/upload, bounded pressure, cancellation, privacy, and zero-owned-resource cleanup pass.
./LOGBOOK.md:120:- OWNER DECISION: `owner-approved-m0-vs-release-gate-decoupling.md` makes accepted physical-Mac smoke `TASK-260715-9yp8to` the technical prerequisite and keeps the blocked Apple account evidence APC34W-B1–B3 as a release-only gate. No release-readiness pass is inferred.
./LOGBOOK.md:134:- VERIFICATION: Focused Swift Testing covers first use, same/different key, invalid label with identical bytes, malformed key, sequential rotation generations, one-active-approval validation, revocation, canonical-host/port mismatch, unsupported precedence, production composition, and redaction. A loopback libssh2 test proves all untrusted/rejected outcomes keep credential-provider calls, authentication attempts, and destination channels at zero.
./LOGBOOK.md:151:### 1616 — macOS-only Gate P0 passes on the physical Mac (TASK-260715-2ayxqn)
./LOGBOOK.md:153:- GATE DISPOSITION (supersedes the 2026-08-11 blocked reading): Overall macOS-only Gate P0 is PASS. Accepted C1 authority for the Relux Works r12 matrix, exact server-issued device-bound profiles, signed archive inspection, system approval, and physical provider lifecycle directly close every in-scope technical provisioning row. The `TASK-260715-apc34w` membership/agreement/Admin-field gaps remain release/account-assurance obligations and are not inferred closed, but the owner-approved active prototype scope does not treat them as unresolved P0 portal approval.
